---
description: Playwright E2E patterns for Next.js and Fastify API
glob: "apps/next/e2e/**/*, apps/next/playwright.config.ts, apps/fastify/test/**/*, apps/fastify/playwright.config.ts"
---

## Config
- No webServer; URLs from `PLAYWRIGHT_APP_URL` / `PLAYWRIGHT_API_URL` (env or `--app` / `--api` params)
- Fastify: only `--api` param; `test:e2e` = URL-based, `test:e2e:local` = spawn API, poll, run, cleanup
- Param format: `--app=URL` or `--app URL`, `--api=URL` or `--api URL`
- CI: test:e2e:local (spawn local). Optional: Vercel previews with `VERCEL_AUTOMATION_BYPASS_SECRET`, `ALLOW_TEST=true` for preview
- Local: Next `test:e2e:local` = spawn Fastify + Next, poll, run, kill. Fastify `test:e2e:local` = spawn API only. Root `pnpm test:e2e` = run both via scripts/run-e2e.mjs
- workers: 1, fullyParallel: false — PGLite does not support concurrent writers; tests must run in series
- projects: auth first (`magic-link-auth.spec.ts`), chromium second (all other specs including `wallet-auth.spec.ts`, `link-wallet.spec.ts`, `link-email.spec.ts`)

## Session Model
- Context = browser profile; authenticatedPage = single shared page reused across all authed tests (worker-scoped)
- One login per worker, then navigate and assert. No per-test login for authed tests
- Session reused via worker-scoped storageState (saved after login, new context per test)
- **Exception — wallet specs**: `wallet-auth.spec.ts`, `link-wallet.spec.ts`, `link-email.spec.ts` intentionally perform `authHelpers.sendMagicLink` + `verifyMagicLink` per test (do not use `authenticatedPage`); this diverges from the worker-scoped session pattern

## Test Order
- Auth project first: error tests, then login/logout tests (ends with logout)
- Chromium project: unauth tests first (logged-out state), then first authed test triggers fixture (login) and confirms session, then all remaining authed tests run consecutively
- Authed tests must run consecutively — no unauth test between them

## Wallet Extension Specs
- `wallet-metamask-auth.spec.ts`, `wallet-solana-auth.spec.ts`: use `testWithSynpress(metaMaskFixtures|phantomFixtures(setup))` instead of `@playwright/test`; real wallet connect + sign, no mocks
- Before running wallet extension specs: run `pnpm synpress:metamask` and `pnpm synpress:phantom` (or `pnpm synpress:build`). Cache in `.cache-synpress`; add to `.gitignore`
- CI and `test:e2e:local` must build Synpress cache when wallet specs are in scope

## Auth Fixtures
- Login/logout tests: import `@playwright/test`, use `page` (fresh context per test)
- Authed feature tests: import from `e2e/fixtures`, use `authenticatedPage`; no `loginAsTestUser` in test body
- Wallet specs: use `authHelpers.sendMagicLink` + `verifyMagicLink` per test (exception to Session Model); do not use `authenticatedPage` fixture
- Each authed test must navigate to its target route (e.g. `authenticatedPage.goto('/')`) since the same page is reused

## Test Email
- Use `test@test.ai` when `ALLOW_TEST` enabled; token from DB (`/test/magic-link/last`), no fake outbox. Unit tests with `setTestEmailProvider` can use any email; only E2E magic-link flow requires `@test.ai`.
